write_root_readiness_scripts() {
  mkdir -p "$workspace/scripts"
  write_file "$workspace/FEARLESS_PROJECT_PLAN.md" \
    "# FEARLESS Project Plan" \
    "" \
	    "Last updated: 2026-08-24" \
	    "## 2026-08-23 Taira first-release contract hardening" \
	    'Established one non-compatibility Taira identity: `fc56984b-2be7-431d-840e-21514d1883f0`, `6TEAJqbb8oEPmLncoNiMRbLEK6tw`, `xor#universal`, and decimal scale `9`; every wallet rejects the retired `iroha3-taira` identifier.' \
	    'Wallets fail closed on incomplete routed fanout, derive precision from `spec.scale`, return a fee-unavailable error, never a fabricated zero-fee quote, and require a matching terminal `Applied` receipt.' \
	    'The live snapshot observed build `7efcc118eb50e3369d004d092f9b9d0b4d31ac52`, two peers, one of five routed asset reads succeeding, canonical XOR with a null scale, and zero of four committed validator names resolving.' \
	    'No live deployment, reset, DNS change, funded write canary, or external publication was performed; release requires the full live gate passes against that exact commit.' \
	    "### 2026-07-11 Android Iroha Core Staging And Release-Handoff Hardening" \
	    'The current owner-approved 116,231,129-byte republished release ZIP is pinned to SHA-256 `50e37369e3b08e4435f15ae31d1baca28dd55eae82686000df8f39b85feee7e6`; its JAR SHA-256 `33f449700948641c73eeaa4e4a8ab9e39d3d6a642a50b6b7d8c30a9f6aff19ce`.' \
	    "The materializer passed 63 negative/adversarial scenarios." \
	    "The staged bridge passed eight Java tests and one Kotlin isolation test; its independent compact-hash verifier passed 29 adversarial scenarios and 11 ULEB128 boundaries." \
	    "The Android blocked-readiness self-test passed 39 destructive fixtures." \
	    'Native Taira XOR is exactly `6TEAJqbb8oEPmLncoNiMRbLEK6tw` at scale `9`; `61CtjvNd9T3THAR65GsMVHr82Bjc` may coexist only as a secondary fixture. The observed build `7efcc118eb50e3369d004d092f9b9d0b4d31ac52` has canonical scale `null` with one of five routed asset reads succeeding; the SDK tag points at `4f8cfbdd17aa6a3b049e619f23ec02501e5297b6`.' \
	    'Android production send remains **Blocked** under `android_staged_bridge_production_gates_required`. Production DI still uses `UnavailableIrohaTransferSigner`; the staged bridge is not an app dependency.' \
	    'Release handoff requires the canonical `/run/secrets/passkey-smoke-grant-helper` as a readable executable; every PI deployment/smoke handoff uses the root-pinned Yarn runner; root release readiness retained 194 scenarios plus three production override-injection checks.' \
	    '### 2026-07-11 iOS Iroha Assessment And Upstream Compact Codec Closure' \
	    'The archive review covered all 20 entries and recorded `392660196` compressed bytes, `1396110349` expanded bytes, `704780504` maximum entry, and ratio `3.556`. The iOS self-test passes 74 negative/adversarial fixtures and the root catalog adds 58 independent mutations.' \
	    'iOS production send remains **Blocked** under `apple_xcframework_review_and_materialization_required`. The app supports iOS `14.1` while the SDK requires `15.0`; all three published slice hashes disagree. The local Swift compact correction is unpublished, unreviewed, and diagnostic only.' \
	    'At current upstream base `d6081aa2ce5c50c9a143a24e37d808e02ed1ebe4`, SCCP V1 is a closed ETH/BSC/TRON corridor. Solana and TON are outside SCCP V1 and are rejected. The historical `sccp_ton_taira_xor_deploy.mjs` and governed TON helpers are intentionally retired. Their replacements are the `sccp_release_common.py` bundle/verifier/readiness tools plus the `evidence-scripts` and `js-sdk` corridor phases; production release tooling contains no signing or deployment API.' \
	    'The checked-in `NoritoBridge.xcframework` reports ABI 8 while the loader minimum is ABI 14 and current Rust source is ABI 17.' \
	    'ABI-17 source/header parity now proves an exact 22-export recursive C inventory. Swift availability requires all 21 proof/protocol symbols and independently checks the free symbol without an unsafe cast. JavaScript header/export parity passes 76/76 and the focused Swift V2 slice passes 3/3.' \
	    'Local `@iroha/iroha-js` `0.0.3` exposes the browser codec with strict uncofactored Ed25519 verification. Its focused release boundary passes 96/96 and the codec/crypto adversarial selection passes 45/45; the aggregate/SHA focus passes 10/10 and the affected regression selection passes 207/207. Node 18.20.8, 20.20.2, 22.23.1, 24.18.0, and 26.5.0 each pass 2,570 of 2,644 tests with 74 skips; one parallel result is excluded from release evidence. The current enforced Torii ceiling is 840 KiB; the browser codec was measured at 125,424 bytes / 36 modules / zero forbidden inputs / 122.5/132 KiB; and the browser Nexus app at 197,732 bytes / 45 modules / zero forbidden inputs / 193.1/205 KiB remain enforced. The public browser aggregate is 284,780 bytes (278.1/300 KiB), 46 modules, zero forbidden Node inputs, and zero global-Buffer assignments; missing esbuild fails closed. The exact bundle inventory now has seven targets; all six browser targets require both graph guards. For the accepted b423 candidate, the exact pinned-esbuild Torii measurement is 853,208 bytes across 57 modules under the unchanged 840 KiB (860,160-byte) cap, leaving 6,952 bytes (0.81%) of headroom. Its complete public browser aggregate is 303,924 bytes across 51 modules, with zero forbidden Node inputs and zero global-Buffer assignments, under the unchanged 300 KiB (307,200-byte) cap, leaving 3,276 bytes (1.08%) of headroom. The remote Kotodama compiler is exactly 51,000 bytes (49.8 KiB) against the 51 KiB (52,224-byte) cap, six modules, zero forbidden inputs, and zero global-Buffer assignments, leaving 1,224 bytes (2.40%) of headroom.' \
	    'Signer callbacks now receive only detached canonical Transfer::Asset signables; alias conflicts and all wait options fail before signer/Torii side effects, and raw iterable entries count before deduplication.' \
	    'The post-hardening package subset passes 138/138. Fresh ephemeral Playwright WebKit QA against the final package passes 56 adversarial/runtime scenarios and 183 assertions with zero failures, console errors, or warnings. Its 807,975-byte unminified bundle has 57 esbuild input modules, zero forbidden graph inputs, and no global Buffer. The temporary harness is not committed/replayable.' \
	    'The final post-prepare `0.0.3` candidate was packed twice byte-identically at 154 files/archive entries, 1,277,584 packed bytes, and 7,901,798 unpacked bytes, with npm SHA-1 shasum `9b0246d3e30b0bb9e9fbf5b41b7f825703640c2f`, tar SHA-256 `6e5f806cc42d12f43a97f56688d335fe07931376f18300c8fa83a915a519653b`, and SHA-512 integrity `sha512-f46HkUK6tc5rtSeFLTOnjY9MDMVKIAVtv0GOUlDMOHLvEF1G+LPfmpzlOAJyQOnbHIuT/tS3x3dtLQ9n3BD5OQ==`.' \
	    'The shared vector payload prehash `e673f611d9d42b02f5c1ff55ec6c2133c51b9a20be1f4eaa84f32ed9ffb2c395` and canonical hash `2332d0004eb24d97fd965fe68f6f31b0e51339764b4dd80f3ea50a3b6f7e5003` are asserted in Rust, JavaScript, Kotlin, Java, Swift, and Python. Canonical, Android, Swift, and Python transaction-fixture families are exactly aligned at 27 entries each. Fixture consumers require canonical base64 and exact source/manifest sets and reject duplicate names, encoded files, payload hashes/bytes, and signed hashes/bytes before name-keyed collapse.' \
	    'Stable `cargo check -p iroha_core` now passes after a handler-table no-mutation regression (1/1), with 28 non-fatal pre-existing dead-code warnings. `cargo fmt --all -- --check` passes with no remaining compile or formatting blocker.' \
	    'Final Kagemusha V2 policy/Torii closure is green: 12/12 durable Torii-focused tests, 3/3 Core global-operation-ID tests, and 76/76 JavaScript static ABI-parity tests passed. `cargo check -p iroha_torii` has zero errors and 28 existing Core warnings; test-profile builds expose 31 warnings. The main policy and all 12 affected destructive mode groups passed, including 17 OpenAPI mutations and 15 smoke mutations. Canonical OpenAPI verification uses the documented `--allow-unsigned` fallback. V2 redeem remains fail closed until a canonical atomic operation-receipt backend exists.' \
	    'The final `@iroha/iroha-js` `0.0.3` source is committed and pushed in PR `hyperledger-iroha/iroha#5618` at exact head `555b2bc06cee90c3375a448bff8d0af8153af3b8`, tree `6df598cfcd5baab82379bac1455dd739ed4cf47d`, over base `8a54f8ea3e94f6ba2b341d4a03718fa9e99ea8cc`. DCO is green and an independent review found no findings, but protected review, merge, publication, and wallet pinning remain open. Immutable `0.0.2` remains pinned, so `browser_transaction_codec_unpublished_source_only` remains until the reviewed immutable codec artifact is published and pinned.' \
	    '| Production Iroha send codecs are not integrated | Open | Android archive/hash review and a core-only Java bridge test stage are complete under `android_staged_bridge_production_gates_required`; the bridge remains outside app/runtime DI. iOS archive path/type/encryption/CRC/bomb-bound review passed, but app/SDK minimums are iOS 14.1/15.0 and production gates remain open. Iroha JS PR `#5618` now preserves the final source at immutable head `555b2bc06cee90c3375a448bff8d0af8153af3b8`, but protected review, merge, package publication, and wallet pinning remain open, so `browser_transaction_codec_unpublished_source_only` remains. |' \
	    "| Deploy the current PI cryptographic health/state/RPC trust contract to production | Blocked |" \
	    "| Release-readiness implementation PRs are not merged | Open | \`config/release-readiness-prs.tsv\` now tracks 36 release-PR requirements. Iroha \`#5611\` and \`#5612\`, Polkaswap deployment-evidence PR \`#1\`, and Polkaswap numeric replay-order hotfix PR \`#3\` are merged with their pinned required checks. Twelve protected-branch blockers remain: \`soramitsu/fearless-Android#1258\`, \`soramitsu/fearless-Android#1259\`, \`soramitsu/fearless-iOS#1301\`, \`soramitsu/fearless-iOS#1302\`, \`soramitsu/shared-features-spm#81\`, \`soramitsu/fearless-wallet-web#1062\`, \`soramitsu/fearless-site-web#49\`, \`tonswap-org/ton-indexer#12\`, \`tonswap-org/ton-indexer#13\`, \`solswap-io/solswap-indexer#16\`, \`sora-xor/polkaswap-indexer#5\`, and \`hyperledger-iroha/iroha#5618\`. Every blocker remains open and requires an eligible reviewer/protected merge. |" \
	    "The latest actual full Polkaswap Vitest run passed 542 tests across 22 files." \
	    'The deployment-evidence suite passed 111 runtime negative assertions: 90 literal `expect_failure` call sites plus 21 additional loop executions.' \
	    "The deterministic evidence-template suite passed 12 negative assertions plus its successful generation control." \
	    "Live PI returns HTTP 400 with exactly four GraphQL validation errors: \`genesisHash\`, \`latestIndexedBlock\`, \`latestIndexedBlockHash\`, and \`latestIndexedAt\`." \
	    'The 2026-07-11 live request to `https://pi.soramitsu.io/graphql` returns HTTP 400 with exactly four GraphQL validation errors: `_health` does not define `genesisHash`, `latestIndexedBlock`, `latestIndexedBlockHash`, or `latestIndexedAt`.' \
	    '`sora-xor/polkaswap-indexer#1` merged into `develop`; `sora-xor/polkaswap-indexer#3` remains review-blocked on `master`, so the reviewed migration fix and deployment evidence must be reconciled before production deployment.' \
	    'The former extra `fearless-utils-Android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties` drift was removed; the exact pinned derived-tree, public-dependency handoff, and strict Android provenance checks now pass.' \
	    'The former extra `fearless-utils-Android` Gradle-wrapper drift was removed.'
  # Exercise the authoritative plan itself. The compact literals above retain
  # mutation-target compatibility for older catalog sections, while this copy
  # prevents their historical evidence snapshot from becoming the baseline.
